  "review_state": "reviewed",
  "contract": "A run's cooperative cancellation delivered at a parallel group with activity members and at a selection handle (published Server 2.11.7, Workflow CooperativeCancellationDelivery::parallelEligibility and WorkflowExecutor::deliverPortableCancellation), over raw worker HTTP on protocol 1.20 in a fresh namespace with a cooperative worker. Each case completes the run's first task with a group, claims the first activity, requests the run's cancellation, delivers it and completes the run. A parallel group of activities, and a mixed group of an activity and a timer, take one parallel delivery whose span names the group; each member is cancelled by its kind, in sequence order (ActivityCancelled, TimerCancelled). A span that does not name the group is a shape mismatch. A selection group of an activity and a timer takes a selection_handle delivery at the next sequence naming its operation range, which cancels both members and records the operation range. The claimed activity's next heartbeat is told to cancel. Embedded applications have no worker protocol.",
